    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to maintain offensive momentum today against Shane Drohan, with **Kyle Tucker** anchoring the lineup as our most viable starter. **Kyle Tucker** carries a score of 63.68, buoyed by his premium slot in the batting order. While the left-on-left matchup against Drohan (3.91 xERA) poses a slight hurdle, **Kyle Tucker**\u2019s elite base projection and recency provide enough buffer to retain his status as a \"Strong\" play. **Andy Pages** also finds his way into the starting utility spot with a 53.07 score; although his position as the assumed #7 hitter limits his RBI ceiling, he remains a viable pivot given the current state of our bench and the need for daily cap management.\n\nThe most difficult decision for today's optimizer centered on **Liam Hicks**, who finished just shy of the 40-point floor at 39.61. **Liam Hicks** benefited from a positive platoon split against right-handed pitcher Williams, but the matchup against an elite 2.95 xERA arm suppressed his overall output enough to keep him on the bench. Similarly, **Brayan Rocchio** was relegated to the pine with a 38.88 score; despite his potential for stolen bases\u2014a critical asset for our strategy\u2014the combination of an unfavorable 3.62 xERA pitcher and a projected #9 spot in the order rendered him too risky to start under our current efficiency protocols. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains unavailable due to his IL designation, further tightening our starting options.",
